title: showing complex in-tree relationships
pid: 6e9e027b-45d7-4f5d-8b2c-0a3238ada88f
body: |2-
  Already established: a is parent, b is grandparent, etc.
  New: <1> is children, <2> is grandchildren;
  <1:1> is the first child, <1:2> the second child,
  <1:3..> is the third child and every child thereafter.
  (So <1> could also be written <1..>.)
  <1:1 / 1> is all children of the first child,
  <1:1 / 1:2> is the second child of the first child, etc.
